G0482.def:
**ἀντι-λαμβάνω **
[frequently in LXX for חָזַק hi., סָמַךְ, etc ;]
to take instead of or in turn. Mid., with genitive, to take hold of;
(a) **of persons, to help **(see MM, _VGT_, see word): [[Luk.1.54|Luk.1:54]], [[Act.20.35|Act.20:35]];
(b) **of things, to partake of**: [[1Ti.6.2|1Ti.6:2]] (see Field, _Notes_, 210; Cremer, 386; and cf. συν-αντιλαμβάνω).†
(AS)

G0467.def:
**ἀντ-απο-δίδωμι**
(ἀντί ἀποδίδωμι), [in LXX for שָׁלַם pi., גָּמַל, שׁוּב hi., etc. ;]
**to give back as an equivalent, recompense, requital **(the ἀντί ex­pressing the idea of full, complete return; see Lft., _Notes_, 46);
(a) **in favourable sense**: [[Luk.14.14|Luk.14:14]], [[Rom.11.35|Rom.11:35]], [[1Th.3.9|1Th.3:9]];
(b) **in unfavourable sense**: [[Rom.12.19|Rom.12:19]], [[2Th.1.6|2Th.1:6]], [[Heb.10.30|Heb.10:30]].†
(AS)
